# Build output and everything a fuzz run generates.
#
# The generated seed corpus is ignored on purpose: it is copied out of
# hmailserver\test at build time by make-corpus.ps1, so committing it would be a
# second copy of ~50 test messages that could then drift from the originals -
# including the two DKIM-signed .eml files, where a drifted copy is worse than no
# copy. The originals stay the single source of truth.
#
# The growing corpus and the crash artifacts are ignored because they are
# machine-local and can reach hundreds of megabytes. When a finding is worth
# keeping, it is *moved* into fuzz\regression\<target>\, which is not ignored -
# see fuzz\regression\README.md.

build/
bin/
corpus/
artifacts/
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.obj
*.exe

# ...but the reproducers and their README are tracked.
!regression/
!regression/**
